**Additional Job Description**
**Core responsibilities as a Manager (PiD Specialist) would entail (but not be limited to)**
As a Manager (PiD Specialist) in the team, you’ll be at the heart of our delivery on some of the most complex and high-profile transactions in the market. You will work closely with colleagues to support with leading client engagements, managing workstreams, and acting as a trusted advisor to client stakeholders.


Drawing on your people expertise, you’ll help organisations navigate critical workforce challenges across the deal lifecycle — from planning and execution to integration and transformation.


You will also play a pivotal role in developing our people, shaping propositions, and driving business development opportunities, ensuring that our practice continues to grow and succeed.


**Your Responsibilities May Include**

* Direct interaction with and ability to build trusted relationships with People leaders and other senior business stakeholders;
* Managing workstream delivery to time, quality, and budget, while providing insight and lessons learned from previous projects;
* Coaching and developing colleagues at all levels, providing feedback and guidance to enhance technical, interpersonal, and consulting skills across the team;
* Working with cross-functional PwC teams to bring integrated solutions to client challenges;
* Driving business development by scoping people related activities on transactions, contributing to proposals, and shaping compelling client propositions;
* Supporting the development of our practice through thought leadership, knowledge sharing, and sector-specific initiatives.

**What You Will Gain**
You will have the opportunity to work alongside a high-performing, UK-based People in Deals team. This collaborative environment will enable you to learn from experienced professionals, share best practices, and contribute directly to global deal-related activities;


By engaging with colleagues across borders, you will gain valuable international exposure, enhance your understanding of global deals and broaden your professional perspective;


The opportunity to take an important role on challenging and complex projects, working directly with client stakeholders;


The chance to deepen your expertise in both the strategic and technical aspects of workforce related issues within a transaction, while also developing your leadership and business development skills;


Exposure to multiple sectors, client types, and deal contexts, giving you a broad and varied career path within PwC;


A supportive and collaborative team environment where you’ll be empowered to take ownership and make an impact;


Ongoing training and development, including opportunities to deepen your consulting skills and specialise in areas of interest.


**Must-have Skills**
Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to engage credibly with the UK PiD team and client stakeholders, managing upwards effectively;


Excellent quantitative and written skills, able to build analyses or an evidence base to support a position, often in situations with imperfect or incomplete information.


Strong analytical skills and data literacy; proficiency in Excel, Power BI, or other data tools is preferred;


Ability to leverage AI and digital tools to enhance analysis, improve efficiency, and deliver innovative solutions to clients.


Ability to manage shifting timelines and ambiguous project environments;


A healthy
**curiosity**
, coupled with a disciplined approach to understanding and
**solving problems**
.


**Comfortable under pressure and managing through ambiguity**
to deliver tasks in an environment where there are many unknowns.


**Adaptable**
, and up for the challenge of mastering new sectors and developing experience across a wide range of subject areas.


**Experience**
Proven success in leading workstream delivery, managing priorities, and producing high-quality outputs ideally under the pressures of a deal environment;


Some experience of working on deals (integration, carve-out, or post-deal), ideally combined with broader business transformation experience and a people focused background;


Experience in coaching, mentoring, and performance managing teams to support with the continuous improvement of capability and performance;


Experience in consulting or professional services would be advantageous, but not essential.


**Eligibility Criteria**

* Past Experience: 5+ years of prior relevant work experience.
* Some experience in M&A or management consulting domain would be advantageous.

**Overview**
Waters, the world's leading specialty measurement company that cares about inclusion and diversity is seeking for a
**Chemistry Account Manager**
to support the very successful growth of our businesses across
**Mumbai Territory in West Region**
Waters deliver benefits through innovation and people that enable customer success in the life, materials and food sciences.
**People create the Waters difference.**
By engaging with our talented and diverse workforce we continuously evolve, develop and improve our products. We believe in delivering innovative technology and system solutions to our valued customers to enable their success.


Customer success have been the motive in driving the consumable business, as it is always at the forefront of the customer supporting them in every workflow of Method development as well as trouble shooting their day to day challenges and providing a total solution in a broad area of applications, its not only limited to Pharmaceuticals, Food, Chemical or Health science market, but into a very diversified field.


You are an ambassador of Waters and will bring to the market Waters’ products and services. You will demonstrates a clear grasp of understanding the customers’ business and its growth plans, as well as be able to take the knowledge and convert that into a solution and offering from Waters, with a primary aim of bringing “customer success”. This position brings you a great degree of flexibility working in the field. Your role will be designated to either a territory and/or markets.


Responsibilities: Achieve the organizational objectives and sales goals.


Addressing new and existing customers in diverse markets with Waters Consumable Products


Maintaining and developing existing customer and identifying and developing new accounts;


Regularly visiting customers within the assigned territory;


Organizing, delivering and following up seminars and workshops at customer sites;


Providing customers with high quality technical advice whilst maintaining a focus on maximizing the sales potential;


Collaborating, liaising and providing guidance and support across departments to ensure customer success. You will be working closely with all other groups at Waters (e.g. Instrument Sales, Application team, Product & Market management team and Informatics etc.);


Formulating and successfully implementing business plans;


Planning and prioritizing personal time and sales activities;


Adhering to Waters and customers relevant Health, Safety and Environment requirements when on site and as an individual employee;


Using related systems, e.g. CRM, Sales Force, Quotation system, with a keen mind on improvements and upgrades.


